data.content:
The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package upgraded from **OpenAPI.NET v1 to v2** (`Microsoft.OpenApi 2.x`). This is a major breaking change in the underlying library. Here's what changed and how to fix each piece:

---

## 1. `OpenApiString` and `IOpenApiAny` removed

OpenAPI.NET v2 uses `JsonNode` instead of `IOpenApiAny` types.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After (.NET 10)
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

Remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;` — that namespace no longer exists.

---

## 2. `OpenApiResponse` → responses are now keyed differently

`operation.Responses` changed from `OpenApiResponses` (a dictionary subclass) to `IDictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>`. The `TryAdd` call still works, but ensure you're not using any removed helper methods. Your line is likely fine as-is:

```csharp
operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });
```

---

## 3. `OpenApiReference.Type` → `OpenApiReference` restructured

`ReferenceType` enum and the `Type` property were removed. References now use the `Id` directly with the collection context.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};

// After (.NET 10)
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme();
oAuthScheme.Ref = "oauth2";  // or use a document reference
```

Or use the new reference pattern:

```csharp
var oAuthScheme = OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
```

The exact API depends on your version — the pattern is now `new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2")`.

---

## 4. `schema.Nullable` removed

In OpenAPI v3.1 (which v2 of the library targets), `nullable` is no longer a property. Instead, `type` is an array that can include `"null"`.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (.NET 10)
// To remove nullable: remove "null" from the Type flags
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;

// To make nullable:
property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

`Type` is now a `[Flags] enum JsonSchemaType` rather than a string.

---

## 5. `schema.Required` is now `ISet<string>` → no change needed

The `Contains` call still works.

---

## Summary of using directives

```csharp
// Remove:
// using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;

// Add:
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;
```

---

## Fixed code

```csharp
options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

The core theme: OpenAPI.NET v2 aligns with **OpenAPI 3.1 / JSON Schema 2020-12**, so `IOpenApiAny` → `JsonNode`, `Nullable` → type flags, and references use dedicated `*Reference` classes.
